                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %ul
            %li#Bredon67b
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Glen+Bredon"}> Glen Bredon
              , Section I.1. of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Equivariant+cohomology+theories"} Equivariant cohomology theories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0082690"} doi:10.1007/BFb0082690
          %p announced in
          %ul
            %li#Bredon67a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Glen+Bredon"}> Glen Bredon
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant cohomology theories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.bams/1183528794"} educlid:1183528794
          %p
            In the broader generality of general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
            and specifically of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Whitehead+theorem"} equivariant Whitehead theorem
            is due to:
          %ul
            %li#Matumoto71
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Takao+Matumoto"}> Takao Matumoto
                ,
                = succeed "," do
